       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, is 16,000 mg/day. That's roughly five times the maximum ibuprofen dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. In a 70 kg adult it could cause severe GI bleeding, kidney failure, metabolic acidosis, and seizures. Confirming it doesn't give me a clinical reason to think it's intended, and an order like this could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right now**, such as 400 mg or 800 mg PO four times daily, or 600 mg every 6 hours.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, for example scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n- **Check it with pharmacy or your attending** if you think there's an unusual reason for this dose. If they confirm it, it can go through their channels.\n\nIf the \"4000\" was a typo for 400 mg, tell me and I'll enter that order now."
      }
     ],
